  "answer": "Project Zenith is a data analytics initiative launched by Alex with a $500,000 Phase 1 budget led by Sarah Tan. The project has secured a strategic partnership with TechInnovate, expanded its team with five new members (including Mike Chen and Lisa Ray) specializing in cybersecurity, cloud architecture, and machine learning, and recently reached a major milestone with a successfully tested secure file sharing prototype. Initial findings suggest a 20% efficiency increase via AI algorithms, with a meeting scheduled for August 5th to discuss these results. The project is moving into a development phase led by Omar Jensen, with UI enhancements planned for October and new security protocols (MFA and encryption) effective next January. Additionally, a $15,000 training budget has been approved for the coding team and project managers, starting next month."
